            <ArticleTitle>[Lipid metabolic characteristics of young adults with ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>59-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lipid metabolism was studied in 166 patients under 40 years of age suffering from myocardial infarction. Marked changes were revealed in the condition of lipid metabolism: hyperlipoproteinemia, hypercholesterolemia, hypertriglyceridemia, increased level of free fatty acids. In some cases, atherosclerosis of the coronary arteries was confirmed by the results of selective coronarography; hyperlipidemia was found more frequently than changes in the coronarograms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
